Z||000000||Alex2004||07-23-2001||10:58 PM||||Earlier i had just got done washing my car, and was going to go to my friends, on my way over there Only a few blocks) i see smoke ( i thought steam) coming from my right rear vent. So i turned down some other road because a few things went through my head and then went on to my friends because the smoke had stopped, as i pulled up the car started acting wierd and then the check engine light came on and i shut it off, then i went in a talked to my friend for a sec and then we walked out to my car b/c i told him what happened, when i opened my door, smoke came out and i smelled major electric burn. and then i took off myconsole thing bc i thought it might have been my ecm, then his step dad comes out and looks and my alernator wire right by the battery, it looked like it had been taped before though. So he taped it up and i drove it home.  Do you think i need a new alterntor? Because that kidna freaked my out!also, when i start it, the rpm's will go up, like normal, and then it will almost die if i don't give it gas (most of the time) and when i got back home from my friends when i shut the car off, i heard kinda a grinding sound, i'm not sure what it was, but it sounded crappy... how much do new alternators cost?  it's for an 84 SE.  Do any of you know what might have caused this?... Let me know... thanks<P>I just went outside and was going to put my console back on and i looked downa nd some of the insulation was burnt!!! i gotta get a fire extinguisher!  Why would the ecm get so hot?<BR>Alex...  <A HREF="mailto:Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com">Abercrombiealex15@hotmail.com</A>  <p>[This message has been edited by Alex2004 (edited 07-23-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||DecadenceR||07-24-2001||01:02 AM||||To me it sounds like you need to replace the positive battery wire. As for the melted insulation on the ECM, I'm not sure about that one.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Alex2004||07-24-2001||12:58 PM||||Today i went outside and was looking at my ECM and the white plug on the left (facing it) had some black stuff on it like from a fire, not melted though, and i can see where the isulation was burned on the ECM, is there some way i can take it apart or something to see if it's messed up on the inside?  I drove it back from my friend's last night and the lights and everything worked like it's supposed to.  Is there anything i can do to see if i need to get a new one?  And is all of this because of the Alternator wire by the battery????  This is the first time this has ever happened to me so i am clueless.  Let me know...<P>Alex...||||reg||11
Z||000003||sqoach||07-24-2001||01:06 PM||||It doesn't really sound like you need an alternator. But if you do, I've got one.<P>Are you trying to take off the center console? If so, you take off the shifter console first. Take out those 4 screws under the ash trays. Take off the shift knob, and remove the console. Then you'll see 2 screws holding the center console down. And there's 2 more behind the glove box thingy. Then it just lifts out.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">   <P>84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR>86 SC (FOR SALE)<BR>86 SE V6 (new project)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex2004||07-24-2001||01:30 PM||||I have already taken my console out, i didn't need to take the gear shift thing out b/c the console i have, the plastic where the 2 screws that hold it down in the front have been broken.  So i just took the screws out that mount the console onto the ecm, and i carefully slid it out.  <P>Alex...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tigger||07-24-2001||02:01 PM||||That wire from the alternator burnt up on my '84 SE.<P>Previous owner/mechanic had hacked into the engine harness and routed a ton of current (I don't know why) through that little wire which was made up of about 3 pieces of wire put together with household electrical twistee connectors.  It created a gob of resistance and burnt up.  When it was burning up, the car acted strange like you described.<P>I would fix the the alt. wire first and then keep an eye on the wires near the ECM.  I'm thinking those got hot when the alt. wire was burning up but not 100% sure.<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 07-24-2001).]||||reg||1
